                      (    forth6809.asm):12040         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
                      (    forth6809.asm):12041         ; TSTSTRPARSE - strings & parsing tests (glossary section 3.12,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12042         ; 16 words, 19 tests since several get separate cases: [CHAR]
                      (    forth6809.asm):12043         ; compiling/interpreting state, S" compiling/interpreting state
                      (    forth6809.asm):12044         ; (this word genuinely has both), SEARCH found/not-found,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12045         ; REPLACES/SUBSTITUTE combined across two tests (covering all 4
                      (    forth6809.asm):12046         ; of SUBSTITUTE's own documented %-delimiter cases), SNAME
                      (    forth6809.asm):12047         ; found/not-found.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12048         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12049         ; . has no STATE check at all in its own code (confirmed by
                      (    forth6809.asm):12050         ; reading it directly - matches "no interpretation semantics,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12051         ; per ANS" without a specific -14 throw, unlike [CHAR]/S"), so
                      (    forth6809.asm):12052         ; only its compiling case is tested. Its own runtime calls TYPE
                      (    forth6809.asm):12053         ; internally, so its own test applies the SERIALPOLL-conditional
                      (    forth6809.asm):12054         ; lesson from section 3.1 from the start, rather than
                      (    forth6809.asm):12055         ; re-discovering it via a failed MAME run.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12056         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12057         ; SUBSTITUTE/REPLACES/UNESCAPE all carry extensive prior-session
                      (    forth6809.asm):12058         ; bug-fix history in their own comments - confirmed fresh against
                      (    forth6809.asm):12059         ; the actual current code (not re-derived from scratch), and
                      (    forth6809.asm):12060         ; SUBSTITUTE's own expected outputs independently simulated in
                      (    forth6809.asm):12061         ; Python against the traced algorithm before writing the tests,
                      (    forth6809.asm):12062         ; not hand-derived and assumed correct.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12063         ;
                      (    forth6809.asm):12064         ; Note: this section's own COMPARE (string comparison) word's
                      (    forth6809.asm):12065         ; test is named TSTSCOMPARE, not TSTCOMPARE - the latter was
                      (    forth6809.asm):12066         ; already taken by section 3.7's own comparison-operators group
                      (    forth6809.asm):12067         ; wrapper, caught by the standard collision check before
                      (    forth6809.asm):12068         ; insertion.
                      (    forth6809.asm):12069         ; ------------------------------------------------------------
