                      (    forth6809.asm):19666                                  ; elsewhere in this file), so BPL was always
                      (    forth6809.asm):19667                                  ; testing CLR's result, not n1's actual sign.
                      (    forth6809.asm):19668                                  ; BPL always branched, meaning n1 was NEVER
                      (    forth6809.asm):19669                                  ; negated even when genuinely negative - found
                      (    forth6809.asm):19670                                  ; via MAME: TSTMSTAR's two returned values
                      (    forth6809.asm):19671                                  ; came back wrong, which turned out to be
                      (    forth6809.asm):19672                                  ; this, not a push-order swap in the test
                      (    forth6809.asm):19673                                  ; itself. FMSLASHMOD/SMSLASHREM already do
                      (    forth6809.asm):19674                                  ; this correctly (explicit TST PRODHI between
                      (    forth6809.asm):19675                                  ; their own CLR calls and the branch) - MSTAR
                      (    forth6809.asm):19676                                  ; was simply missing the equivalent re-test.
